  "note": "Triennial election of the electoral divisions of Downpatrick rural district, one member each, polled on 2 June 1949. The News-Letter reports contests at Ballynahinch and Ardglass, where the Nationalists gained a seat from Labour. Ballynahinch Rural is recorded from reports of the new council's annual meeting of 11 June 1949, with its division from the 1930 return (round 2, 7 Nov 2026)."
